rem Dyalog Programming Contest 2010
rem Task 5: Variable Interest
rem The central bank moves its rate each quarter by a
rem die roll: pips minus 3.5, divided by 10, never
rem below zero. A variable loan takes the rate at the
rem start of each year and re-amortizes the balance.
rem Estimate how the variable loan compares with the
rem fixed one, in five bins of the final difference.

use "001_params"
use "002_buyorrent"
use io
use cli
use numbers
use random
use sequences

argument Input path = "demos/dyalog/2010/data/buyrent.xml"

State = 2010 seed
Params = Input read getparams
Options = array 9.0 10000
Options Params variablerisk print


rem Shares of simulations in which the variable loan
rem is ahead by more than 50000, by more than 25000,
rem within 25000, behind by more than 25000 and
rem behind by more than 50000.
fun variablerisk Options Params
  unpack Start Count = Options
  Sims = Count integer
  Quarters = Params 2 integer // 3
  Rolls = (1 to 6) (Quarters * Sims) choices
  Changes = ((Rolls - 3.5) / 10) (array Quarters Sims) reshape
  return Changes Start Params difference bins
end


rem Final advantage of the variable loan over the fixed
rem one, a lane per column of quarterly rate Changes.
rem Home value, rent, property tax and the parents'
rem loan are the same for both loans and cancel: what
rem remains is the savings from the payment and tax
rem differences, less the difference of the balances.
rem Every lane is a vector element, so the only loop is
rem over months.
fun difference Changes Start Params
  unpack Price Costs Months BankAmt BankRate DadAmt DadRate Infl Tax PropRate SavRate Rent = Params
  Term = Months integer
  Sims = Changes shape 1
  Fixed = BankAmt (BankRate / 1200) ((1 to Term) copy) loan
  Growth = 1 + SavRate / 1200 * (1 - Tax / 100)

  Official = array shape Sims fill Start * 1.0
  Balance = array shape Sims fill BankAmt * 1.0
  Saving = array shape Sims fill 0.0
  Rate = Official / 1200
  Payment = Balance Rate Term payment
  for Month in 0 till Term
    if Month greater 0 and Month % 12 equal 0
      Rate = Official / 1200
      Payment = Balance Rate (Term - Month) payment
    end
    Interest = Balance * Rate
    Principal = Payment - Interest
    Balance = Balance - Principal
    Flow = (Interest - Fixed .int Month) * Tax / 100 - (Payment - Fixed .pmt)
    Saving = Saving * Growth + Flow
    if Month % 3 equal 2
      Official = (Official + Changes (Month // 3)) 0.0 max
    end
  end
  return Saving - (Balance - Fixed .bal (Term - 1))
end


rem The standard amortization payment for each lane,
rem an equal share of the balance at a zero rate.
rem Sums of quarterly steps can leave a rate a rounding
rem error above zero, where 1 + Rate is exactly 1, so
rem a rate below 1e-9 counts as zero.
fun payment Balance Rate Months
  Annuity = Balance * Rate / (1 - (1 + Rate) ** -Months)
  Zero = Rate less 0.000000001
  return Zero (Balance / Months) Annuity choose
end


fun bins Difference
  Far = (Difference greater 50000) count
  Ahead = ((Difference greater 25000) and (Difference at most 50000)) count
  Even = (Difference abs at most 25000) count
  Behind = ((Difference less -25000) and (Difference at least -50000)) count
  Lost = (Difference less -50000) count
  return (array Far Ahead Even Behind Lost) / (Difference len)
end
